        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-23T20:38:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since any current tooling will have different behavior either way, I think the failure is better. Customers finding out in a month that something changed will still be an escalation + panic to figure out what to do about all the changes that weren\u0027t submitted that they expected to be submitted.\n\nIf you\u0027re that concerned about it, I would start with adding only the log message and not changing the behavior. Then you could reach out to customers proactively if you see log messages. I don\u0027t know how that works from a security release perspective though.",
      "parentUuid": "1f466293_6a3c5fa2",
      "revId": "48c6e20e1f5be0ddb01e000380ec12244d1faa8f",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
